  "_note": "USD per 1M tokens. Prices change — verify on https://www.anthropic.com/pricing and https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing and edit this file. 'match' is a case-insensitive regex tested against the normalized model name; first match wins, so keep specific patterns (e.g. flash-lite) above generic ones. 'context_window' is the effective conversation token limit in Antigravity (~560k for the Gemini 4 family — Antigravity reports maxContextTokens 512000 for them since 2026-11-17 and compacted real conversations at 509k–553k; ~300k for older Gemini, ~168k for Flash-Lite subagents; the native Gemini API window is 'api_context_window'), and 'compaction_threshold' is where Antigravity auto-compacts the history (~505k for Gemini 4, ~250k for older Gemini, ~128k for Flash-Lite, ~840k for Claude 5.5). 'price_changes' entries ({from: 'YYYY-MM-DD', …prices}) apply to calls made on or after that local date. 'service_tiers' (Gemini API batch / flex / priority / contributor) are used only with usage.py --tier; a tier replaces the standard prices together with their price_changes and long_context. Orchestrator (Carbon / Argon / Neon) — a planner that hands its plan to Gemini 4 Hydrogen to carry out — matches its planner's entry; usage.py prices the calls Hydrogen made (Antigravity's metadata names them «Gemini 4 Hydrogen (Orchestrator)»; without it, the plan-mode markers in the transcript tell them apart) at Hydrogen's prices.",
